       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">CRICKET</span> · Crictracker · 2026-10-17 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Afghanistan Captain Rahmat Shah Targets Tri-Series Victory</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#cricket</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Afghanistan captain Rahmat Shah has expressed confidence in his team's ability to win the upcoming ODI tri-nation series in the UAE, scheduled for October 17–23, 2026. Shah cited the team's familiarity with local conditions in Abu Dhabi and Sharjah as a significant competitive advantage over opponents Bangladesh and Zimbabwe.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-17/afghanistan-captain-rahmat-shah-targets-tri-series-victory.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Afghanistan enters the tournament following a hard-fought draw against Bangladesh in a recent one-off Test match, a result Shah believes will boost team momentum. Key players Rashid Khan and Mohammad Nabi return to the squad for the series, reinforcing the team's ambitions for the limited-overs competition.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurate summary of the upcoming series and the captain's confidence. The mention of the draw as a momentum builder is well-supported.</p>
