     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-17 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Andhra Pradesh Launches Life-Saving Irrigation Scheme for Orchards</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The Andhra Pradesh Horticulture Department has introduced the Life-Saving Irrigation (LSI) Scheme to protect orchards in the Sri Sathya Sai district from El Niño-induced heat and water shortages. The government will cover 80% of water costs for farmers whose borewells have dried up.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-17/andhra-pradesh-launches-life-saving-irrigation-scheme-for-or.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Eligible crops, including mango, sweet lime, and arecanut, will receive water via tankers at subsidized rates. To ensure transparency, tankers will be fitted with GPS devices and monitored through a dedicated application. Farmers may apply for the scheme, which covers up to five acres, through their nearest Rythu Bharosa Kendra.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately summarizes the LSI scheme, including the subsidy percentage and eligibility requirements.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/andhra-pradesh/life-saving-irrigation-scheme-launched-to-protect-orchards-in-sri-sathya-sai-district/article71571311.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
