     <article class="story single" data-beat="positive">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">POSITIVE</span> · The Better India · 2026-10-17 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Born with Clubfoot, Shijoy Jacob Cycles Across Countries and Treks Himalayas</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Shijoy Jacob</span> <span>#Clubfoot</span> <span>#Cycling</span> <span>#Trekking</span></div>
       <p>Shijoy Jacob, 38, born with congenital clubfoot, has defied early struggles to walk, cycling across four countries and trekking to 15,000 feet in the Himalayas. His mother, Pushpa, who once worried about his ability to run, now watches him embark on international journeys. Shijoy asserts, &quot;I was born different, but I don't think that should define me and stop my dreams.&quot;</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-17/born-with-clubfoot-shijoy-jacob-cycles-across-countries-and-.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Growing up in Mumbai, Shijoy's legs were twisted inward. His mother made repeated hospital visits, massaged his legs, and left her job to care for him. He underwent surgeries and wore corrective footwear until around age eight. As a child, he felt sad not being able to do what other children did, wondering if he would ever participate.</p><p>By age nine, he stopped wearing heavy footwear and gradually engaged in physical activities. His first 10-kilometre race around 2014-15 marked a breakthrough, building confidence and changing his perspective. This new self-trust opened doors to longer runs, treks, and cycling expeditions, overcoming an initial fear of injury.</p><p>In 2026, Shijoy cycled from Cambodia into Vietnam with three friends, carrying luggage, repairing punctures, and covering over 100 kilometers daily without a support vehicle. He has also cycled through India, Sri Lanka, and Southeast Asia, and completed a Himalayan trek to approximately 15,000 feet. His mother, Pushpa, though still scared, now feels immense pride. Shijoy attributes all credit to his mother, stating, &quot;She is the one because of whom I am here today.&quot;</p><p>Why it matters: Shijoy Jacob's journey highlights the power of perseverance and support in overcoming physical challenges.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft effectively captures the personal narrative of Shijoy Jacob's medical journey and his transition to endurance sports.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://thebetterindia.com/changemakers/shijoy-jacob-born-clubfoot-long-distance-cyclist-himalayas-mumbai-expeditions-12682532" rel="noopener">The Better India</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
