     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-17 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Caste-Based Conferences Surge Ahead of Uttar Pradesh Elections</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Caste-based organisations in Uttar Pradesh are increasing their mobilisation efforts as the state Assembly elections approach. The Parsuram Yuva Jagriti Manch plans to host a large Brahmin community gathering in Shamli district during the last week of October to advocate for increased political representation and the establishment of a Brahmin Welfare Board.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-17/caste-based-conferences-surge-ahead-of-uttar-pradesh-electio.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Additionally, the Sarv Kushwaha Chetna Sangh has scheduled a conference in Jaunpur for October 28 to address concerns regarding economic upliftment and political representation for the Kushwaha community. These events follow a recent Brahmin-Tyagi-Bhumihar Mahakumbh in Saharanpur, which focused on social reform and community grievances.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Provides a concise, accurate overview of the upcoming caste-based gatherings and their political context as described in the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
