     <article class="story single" data-beat="business">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">BUSINESS</span> · Business Standard · 2026-10-17 · editor 10/10 · 3 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>ICICI Bank's Q2 Net Profit Rises 20.1% to ₹14,843 Crore Amidst Sector Growth</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#ICICI Bank</span> <span>#Quarterly Results</span> <span>#Banking</span> <span>#Financials</span></div>
       <p>ICICI Bank, India’s second-largest private sector lender, reported a 20.1 per cent year-on-year increase in standalone net profit, reaching ₹14,843 crore for the July-September quarter of FY27. This growth was bolstered by a strong rise in net interest income (NII) and reduced provisions. NII, the difference between interest earned and interest expended, grew 17.7 per cent year-on-year to ₹25,339 crore, according to Business Standard.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-17/icici-banks-q2-net-profit-rises-201-to-14843-crore-amidst-se.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The bank's total loan portfolio expanded by 30 per cent to ₹18.32 trillion as of September 30, 2026. Excluding loans from international branches against FCNR(B) deposits, the portfolio still grew 24.1 per cent. However, the net interest margin (NIM) moderated to 4.18 per cent in Q2FY27, down from 4.30 per cent in the year-ago quarter and 4.36 per cent in the preceding April-June quarter, with negligible benefit from interest on tax refunds during the September quarter.</p><p>Core operating profit, excluding treasury income, increased 21.8 per cent year-on-year to ₹20,805 crore. Non-interest income, excluding treasury income, rose 12.5 per cent to ₹8,277 crore, while fee income saw a 20.1 per cent rise to ₹7,795 crore. Fees from retail, rural, and business banking customers contributed approximately 75 per cent of the total fee income. Operating expenses increased 8.5 per cent year-on-year to ₹12,811 crore, and the bank reported a treasury loss of ₹230 crore in Q2FY27, contrasting with a gain of ₹220 crore in the year-ago period.</p><p>Provisions declined 6.9 per cent year-on-year to ₹851 crore from ₹914 crore, and sequentially fell 32.5 per cent from ₹1,260 crore in Q1FY27. The gross non-performing assets (GNPA) ratio improved to 1.20 per cent as of September 30, 2026, from 1.38 per cent in the June quarter and 1.58 per cent a year earlier. The net NPA ratio also declined to 0.30 per cent. Gross NPA additions were ₹4,833 crore in Q2FY27, with the bank writing off ₹1,592 crore in gross NPAs. Provisioning coverage ratio on non-performing loans stood at 75 per cent, and ICICI Bank held contingency provisions of ₹13,100 crore, alongside an additional standard asset provision of ₹1,283 crore.</p><p>Total advances grew 30 per cent year-on-year to ₹18.32 trillion. The retail and rural loan portfolio saw a 14.8 per cent year-on-year growth, constituting 51.6 per cent of the total loan portfolio. The business banking portfolio expanded by 33.8 per cent, and the domestic corporate portfolio grew 30.6 per cent. Total period-end deposits increased 27.1 per cent year-on-year to ₹20.50 trillion. The bank added 145 branches in the first half of FY27, expanding its network to 7,656 branches. On a consolidated basis, ICICI Bank's net profit was ₹16,333 crore, up 22.3 per cent, with consolidated assets growing 22.6 per cent to ₹32.93 trillion as of September 30, 2026.</p><p>In related banking news, Axis Bank's Q2 net profit rose 38% to ₹7,003 crore, with net interest income growing 12% to ₹15,371 crore and provisions falling 52%, according to Business Standard. HDFC Bank, however, reported a Q2 net profit rise of 4.7% to ₹19,510 crore, with net interest income up 9.7% to ₹34,620 crore and deposits growing 18.8%, though lower treasury gains and higher expenses impacted profit growth, as per Business Standard.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft is thorough, well-structured, and accurately incorporates all key financial figures and comparisons from the provided source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.business-standard.com/companies/quarterly-results/icici-bank-q2-fy27-result-net-profit-rises-22-3-to-16-333-crore-126101700550_1.html" rel="noopener">Business Standard</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
