     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-17 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>INDIA Bloc Stages 'March for Democracy' in New Delhi</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The INDIA bloc held a 'March for Democracy' in New Delhi on October 12, 2026, to protest against the Chief Election Commissioner and alleged electoral irregularities. The Congress party claimed 2.5 lakh participants joined the four-hour demonstration, which moved toward the Supreme Court.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-17/india-bloc-stages-march-for-democracy-in-new-delhi.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Party leaders coordinated the mass mobilization by asking workers to travel to the capital despite police barricades and detentions. General secretary K.C. Venugopal attributed the high turnout to meticulous planning and a recent organizational overhaul of the Congress party machinery.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately summarizes the reported event, figures, and organizational context provided in the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/india-blocs-march-for-democracy-sees-a-massive-mobilisation-effort-by-congress/article71580467.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       <div class="cityguide"><b>City guide</b><p>More on <a href="https://bharatdn.com/city/new-delhi/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">New Delhi</a> - census 2011 population, live weather and air quality, local food and getaways.</p></div>
