     <article class="story single" data-beat="sports">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">SPORTS</span> · NDTV Sports · 2026-10-17 · editor 8/10 · 2 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>India vs West Indies 5th T20I Toss Delayed by Rain in Bengaluru Amid Series Decider</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Cricket</span> <span>#India vs West Indies</span> <span>#T20I</span> <span>#Bengaluru</span></div>
       <p>The toss for the fifth and final T20I between India and West Indies at the M Chinnaswamy Stadium in Bengaluru on Saturday has been delayed due to rain. With the five-match series tied at 2-2, both teams are vying to clinch the decider, making the weather a critical factor in the outcome. Covers are firmly in place on the pitch as a slight drizzle continues.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-17/india-vs-west-indies-5th-t20i-toss-delayed-by-rain-in-bengal.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>According to an official update, overs will begin to be deducted after 7:45 PM IST, with the latest possible start for a five-over game set for 9:41 PM. Heavy rain has been forecast for Bengaluru, with AccuWeather reporting a 78 percent chance of rainfall around 10 PM IST. While the M. Chinnaswamy Stadium boasts one of the world's best drainage systems, heavy rain could still make conducting a full match difficult.</p><p>India has bolstered its squad with the addition of veteran pacer Bhuvneshwar Kumar, who comes in as injury cover for Arshdeep Singh. Arshdeep was hit on his bowling arm during the previous match in Hyderabad, where India nearly chased down a 248-run target. Bhuvneshwar's inclusion could provide much-needed experience and control, especially given his familiarity with the M Chinnaswamy Stadium, which is his IPL home ground for the Royal Challengers Bengaluru.</p><p>The series has been notably high-scoring, demonstrating how vulnerable even 220-plus totals can be in T20 cricket. West Indies successfully chased 250 in one game, defended 247 by 24 runs in another, and came close to overhauling a 224-run target. This has pushed bowlers to their limits, with India's bowling attack, in particular, facing scrutiny. West Indies star Shai Hope has been a standout performer, hitting four centuries on the tour—two in ODIs and two in T20Is—and contributing significantly to the Windies' three white-ball tour wins when he remained unbeaten, accumulating 539 runs in five games.</p><p>Indian batter Ishan Kishan commented on the team's preparation for the decider, stating it was &quot;somewhere in the middle of both&quot; intense and chilled. He expressed enthusiasm for the high-stakes match, saying, &quot;always a decider match, it comes up with pressure. It comes up with expectations and everything, and this is what we want when we go into bat.&quot; A victory for the West Indies would mark the first time they have beaten India in a T20I series in India since Australia achieved it with a 0-2 win in February 2019.</p><p>What to watch: Monitor weather updates and potential revised match timings for the series decider.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft effectively synthesizes the provided full text and source summary, covering the rain delay, the series context, Ishan Kishan's comments, and the squad updates. It is well-structured and accurate to the provided text.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://sports.ndtv.com/cricket/india-vs-west-indies-live-score-ind-vs-wi-5th-t20i-live-updates-shreyas-iyer-shai-hope-bengaluru-m-chinnaswamy-stadium-12199202#publisher=newsstand" rel="noopener">NDTV Sports</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
