       <h1>India’s Zorawar Tank Faces Two-Year Delay for China Border Deployment</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Defence</span> <span>#Zorawar Tank</span> <span>#Indian Army</span> <span>#China Border</span></div>
       <p>India's indigenous Zorawar tank, intended for deployment along the China border, is facing an estimated two-year delay, as reported by The Economic Times.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-17/indias-zorawar-tank-faces-two-year-delay-for-china-border-de.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The setback is attributed to a new demand from the Indian Army, which has presented significant challenges for the engineers involved in the tank's development.</p><p>This new requirement is testing the capabilities of the engineering teams, pushing back the timeline for the tank's readiness and deployment.</p><p>What to watch: Updates on the engineering challenges and the revised timeline for Zorawar tank deployment.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft effectively conveys the essential details regarding the delay and the reason behind it as reported.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
