     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-17 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Kerala Government Increases Dearness Allowance to 37%</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The Kerala Finance Department issued an order on October 17, 2026, increasing the Dearness Allowance (DA) and Dearness Relief (DR) for government employees and pensioners from 35% to 37%. The increase applies to state employees, teachers, local government staff, and various categories of pensioners.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-17/kerala-government-increases-dearness-allowance-to-37.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The enhanced rates will be disbursed with the November 2026 salary and pension payments. A separate order will be issued regarding arrears effective from November 1. This follows a previous hike earlier this year, which raised the rates from 25% to 35% in February.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief is concise, accurate, and captures all relevant details from the source text.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/kerala/keralam-govt-increases-da-dr-from-35-to-37/article71597567.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
