     <article class="story single" data-beat="cricket">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">CRICKET</span> · Crictracker · 2026-10-17 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Litton Das Demands Improved Batting Consistency Ahead of UAE Tri-Series</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#cricket</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Bangladesh captain Litton Das has challenged his senior batters to improve their consistency as the team prepares for the tri-series against Afghanistan and Zimbabwe, starting October 17 in the UAE. Litton identified the inability to bat full innings in recent ODI series as a critical weakness needing immediate correction.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-17/litton-das-demands-improved-batting-consistency-ahead-of-uae.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Despite the pressure, Litton views the tournament as essential preparation for the 2027 ICC Men's Cricket World Cup and the upcoming Asia Cup. The squad includes newcomer Aliss Al Islam, who earned his maiden call-up following a dominant domestic performance in white-ball cricket.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately summarizes the captain's comments and the team's strategic outlook.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.crictracker.com/cricket-news/litton-das-urges-senior-batters-to-step-up-ahead-of-tri-series-7644/" rel="noopener">Crictracker</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
