     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-17 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Mobile Snatcher Dragged by Passengers on Moving Train in Bihar</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>A mobile snatcher was caught by passengers at Shivnarayanpur Railway Station in Bihar after attempting to steal a phone through a train window. The passengers grabbed the youth's hand and dragged him alongside the moving train until he lost his grip and fell, sustaining injuries.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-17/mobile-snatcher-dragged-by-passengers-on-moving-train-in-bih.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>A viral video captured the incident, which occurred within the Eastern Railway Zone. Following the encounter, the Railway Protection Force took the suspect into custody. While the Chief Public Relations Officer of Eastern Railway confirmed the force apprehended the individual, they noted the footage is old and declined to provide further details.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurate summary of the incident and the CPRO's response, maintaining the requested brevity.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
