     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-17 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Moderate devotee turnout for second day of Dasara festivities</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The second day of Dasara Sarannavaratri festivities at the Indrakeeladri temple in Vijayawada saw a moderate turnout, with 63,370 devotees completing darshan by 1 p.m. on Monday. Traffic remained light until 10 a.m. before gradually increasing as pilgrims arrived to honor the presiding deity, adorned as Sri Gayatri Devi.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-17/moderate-devotee-turnout-for-second-day-of-dasara-festivitie.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Temple authorities implemented advanced crowd-management measures, including AI-enabled cameras, digital displays, and QR-coded wristbands for children. State Endowments Commissioner K. Ramachandra Mohan inspected the facilities, directing staff to ensure food quality and adequate laddu stocks while coordinating with police to maintain safety and minimize inconvenience for visitors.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Covers the turnout and logistical arrangements precisely as provided in the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/andhra-pradesh/moderate-rush-on-the-second-day-of-dasara-festivities-atop-indrakeeladri-in-vijayawada/article71575526.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
