       <h1>NITI Aayog Explores Policies to Boost India's Medical and Dental Device Manufacturing</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#NITI Aayog</span> <span>#Medical Devices</span> <span>#Manufacturing</span> <span>#Healthcare Policy</span></div>
       <p>NITI Aayog is actively exploring policy measures aimed at enhancing India's manufacturing capabilities for medical and dental devices. This initiative seeks to bolster domestic production in a critical healthcare sector.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-17/niti-aayog-explores-policies-to-boost-indias-medical-and-den.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>A recent meeting convened by NITI Aayog included a diverse group of stakeholders, such as domestic manufacturers, government officials, and experts from premier institutions like IIT Delhi and IIT Mumbai. The discussions centered on identifying and addressing key hurdles faced by the industry.</p><p>Extensive discussions highlighted significant challenges, including regulatory hurdles and cost disadvantages that impact Indian manufacturers. The industry body AiMeD underscored these points, emphasizing the urgent need for simpler regulations and robust financial support mechanisms to aid local producers.</p><p>What to watch: Future policy announcements from NITI Aayog regarding these support measures.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft is concise and covers all key aspects of the source material accurately without unnecessary padding.</p>
