       <h1>Telangana Implements El Niño Contingency Plan for Rural Water</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Telangana Minister Danasari Anasuya Seethakka has directed officials to implement a comprehensive summer action plan to ensure uninterrupted drinking water supply amid El Niño concerns. Priorities include completing borewell recharge structures, identifying alternative water sources, and repairing non-functional pumps.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-17/telangana-implements-el-nino-contingency-plan-for-rural-wate.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Officials must prepare for potential reservoir depletion by maintaining 100 emergency pumps and monitoring pipelines to prevent damage during construction. Additionally, the government is promoting short-duration crops for the upcoming season. District collectors have been tasked with enforcing accountability for infrastructure repairs and conducting village-level awareness programs to manage water resources effectively.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief effectively synthesizes the minister's directives and the context of the El Niño contingency planning.</p>
