       <h1>Yo Yo Honey Singh Questioned by Maharashtra Cyber Cell Over Alleged Obscene Remarks</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Yo Yo Honey Singh</span> <span>#Maharashtra Cyber Cell</span> <span>#Obscene Remarks</span> <span>#Concert</span></div>
       <p>Rapper and singer Yo Yo Honey Singh appeared before the Maharashtra Cyber Cell on Friday, October 16, and was questioned for over two hours in connection with a complaint regarding his alleged objectionable remarks. The incident stems from a concert in Delhi in January 2026. The 43-year-old singer was summoned after a Mumbai resident filed a complaint, prompting the Maharashtra Cyber police to register a case and initiate an investigation.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-17/yo-yo-honey-singh-questioned-by-maharashtra-cyber-cell-over-.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Information from the Cyber Cell indicates that Honey Singh had previously been summoned three times but failed to appear, citing his presence abroad. Following these non-appearances, authorities issued another summons directing him to appear on October 16. A senior Cyber Cell official had reportedly warned that the process to issue a Look Out Circular (LOC) could be initiated if he did not comply with the latest summons. Honey Singh attended the questioning on Friday, remaining for over two hours, according to sources, and departed the premises without responding to media inquiries.</p><p>The core of the case relates to alleged obscene remarks made by Honey Singh during a Delhi concert in January 2026. A video clip of the performance subsequently circulated on social media, drawing significant criticism from various users. Earlier reports suggest that the remarks allegedly included an indecent reference to having sex in cars. The online backlash led a Mumbai resident to approach the cyber police with a complaint, resulting in the registration of the current case.</p><p>Following the controversy, Honey Singh issued a video apology, acknowledging that his choice of words had offended people. He explained his intention was to convey a message in a language he believed &quot;Gen Z&quot; would prefer, but expressed deep regret that his expression was &quot;inappropriate and not acceptable to many,&quot; offering his &quot;heartfelt apologies.&quot; The rapper has also faced legal trouble over the controversial track 'Volume 1' with Badshah, with the Delhi High Court ordering its immediate removal.</p><p>What to watch: Further developments in the Maharashtra Cyber Cell's investigation and any subsequent legal actions.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article provides a concise summary of the questioning, the background of the complaint, and the singer's apology.</p>
